(in-ns 'go.arbace.hs) ^{:go/comments [[3 1 "// AOT (HE8, doc/haskell/HASKELL-EVAL-SURVEY.md, \"As built: HE8 (write-ahead)\"): a module's STG compiled to Go over"] [4 1 "// this machine. The generator (GenAOT) compiles each top-level closure of the program's modules as hsi does"] [5 1 "// (compile.go's slots, join points and liveness) and writes its node tree as Go: one Go function per closure body,"] [6 1 "// per case continuation and per join point, each a function of the frame returning the next code to run (the"] [7 1 "// machine's trampoline: runSlice's loop), atoms read from their slots, the frequent pure primops inline, a case"] [8 1 "// on a constructor or a literal a chain of comparisons or a switch, a let's allocations inline. The generated"] [9 1 "// file is part of package hs in the program's build (bin/hsi aot-build): its init registers each closure's"] [10 1 "// installer by the module's key and the closure's name, with the shape of the tree it was generated from. At run"] [11 1 "// time the closure is compiled from its STG as before (the slice keeps the dumps: the declarations, the"] [12 1 "// constructors and the globals come from them) and the installer puts the Go code in place of the tree's code:"] [13 1 "// the closure's body, its nested closures' bodies and its join points' bodies become goCode, its cases' frames"] [14 1 "// continue in Go (CaseE.k), the tree itself kept for the collector's walks (rts.go) and for the nodes the"] [15 1 "// generator leaves to the interpreter (calls, entries, foreign calls). A shape that differs (another dump, another"] [16 1 "// compiler) refuses the installer: the closure runs interpreted."] [29 1 "// goCode is compiled code: a Go function of the frame; orig the node tree it was generated from (the collector's)."] [44 1 "// AOTInstalled and AOTRefused count the closures whose compiled code was installed, and refused (another shape)."] [47 1 "// aotEntered records the top-level closures a run compiled, \"UNIT:MODULE NAME\" (HSI_AOT_MODULES, EnteredModules): the"] [48 1 "// libraries' closures a program needs compiled."] [53 1 "// aotLimit (HSI_AOT_LIMIT=N): only the first N closures installed, the rest interpreted (a bisection of a divergence)."] [61 1 "// aotEnteredFile is HSI_AOT_MODULES's file, a line appended per closure entered (the driver rewrites it sorted at the end)."] [71 1 "// EnteredModules are the closures the run compiled, sorted."] [81 1 "// aotGenerating: the generator compiles closures; nothing is installed meanwhile."] [90 1 "// aotInstall puts a top-level closure's compiled code in place, its tree just compiled (compileTop)."] [95 4 "// written as it grows: a run killed at its CPU limit leaves its list too"] [129 1 "// aotCollect lists a closure's nodes in preorder (a join point's body after the first jump to it, a nested closure's"] [130 1 "// body where its let is) and their atoms: the generator and the installer index them alike."] [191 1 "// aotShape is a digest of a tree's structure: its nodes' kinds, slots and arities, its atoms' kinds and slots."] [243 1 "// ---- helpers of the generated code ----"] [252 1 "// aotApp is App.eval with the function's and the arguments' values read (args in the machine's argument buffer)."] [261 2 "// a class method's selector applied to an evaluated dictionary: the method taken at once"] [288 1 "// aotEnterFun enters fn, of as many arguments as as holds (the argument buffer or its tail), its frame the"] [289 1 "// caller's when the call is a tail call and the caller's frame is large enough."] [299 2 "// (the argument buffer is not cleared: eight values at most, overwritten by the next call)"] [307 1 "// aotDepth is how many compiled functions call each other directly (Go calls in tail positions, HES73) before"] [308 1 "// returning to the trampoline: Go has no tail calls, so the chain is bounded; each bounce of runSlice resets it"] [309 1 "// (HSI_AOT_DEPTH=N another bound, 0 none: a bisection's switch)."] [317 1 "// aotJump runs compiled code next by a direct Go call when the chain allows it (the budget, the stack's limit and"] [318 1 "// the depth checked as the trampoline would), else returns it to the trampoline. Nothing is held on Go's stack"] [319 1 "// across the call: the caller returns what the callee returns."] [329 1 "// CallSite is a known call's callee resolved once (HES73): the call of a global's function, or of a class method"] [330 1 "// selected from a global dictionary (the -O0 programs' every +), cached at its first evaluated sight; state 0 not"] [331 1 "// resolved yet, 1 resolved (fn, its first drop arguments dropped), 2 left to aotApp."] [338 1 "// aotCallG is the call of global g's value to args: by the call site's resolved callee when its arity is the call's,"] [339 1 "// else aotApp's paths."] [352 1 "// aotResolve resolves a call site when its callee is evaluated: a global's function, or a selector's method of a"] [353 1 "// global dictionary (args[0] a global: the same value at every call); an unevaluated callee is resolved later."] [427 1 "// ---- the generator ----"] [429 1 "// GenAOT compiles closures to Go: every one of the program's modules (unit main, every dump of prog) and the"] [430 1 "// libraries' sel names (\"UNIT:MODULE\" the module's every closure, \"UNIT:MODULE NAME\" one; the modules loaded as a run"] [431 1 "// loads them, from their images when the machine has them), one file per module into out, aot_UNIT_MODULE.go; it"] [432 1 "// returns the closures compiled and those refused (a closure hsi cannot compile, its reason)."] [437 39 "// a module's closures named, nil for all"] [515 3 "// a package of its own (arbace/aot/ID): a library module's is compiled once by Go's build cache"] [526 1 "// catch runs f, a panic of the loader or the compiler returned as an error."] [563 30 "// a capture's type and its expression in the installer"] [565 18 "// the functions' names, declared first"] [566 18 "// their definitions"] [567 18 "// the tree's places they are put in, after every definition"] [569 25 "// the addresses of the string literals and labels the machine made"] [572 2 "// typed: the slots whose value the current Go function holds in a typed Go local (HES73: an unlifted binder of"] [573 2 "// an inline primop's result), and whether env holds it too (written at a flush, before anything reads env)"] [577 1 "// tloc is a typed local: its Go name, its type ('I' int64, 'W' uint64, 'D' float64), whether env[slot] has it."] [596 1 "// node is the captured node of index k, typed."] [615 1 "// closure is the Go of a top-level closure: its registration and its installer."] [637 2 "// the captures are the fields of a struct and every function a method of it: functions of their own for Go's"] [638 2 "// compiler (closures in one installer made one huge function of a large closure: 5.6 GB to compile)"] [658 1 "// def notes a write of env[k]: a typed local of k no longer its value."] [661 1 "// flush writes the typed locals env does not hold into env, before the frame is read by other code (a pushed case's"] [662 1 "// continuation, a join point, the interpreter)."] [679 1 "// saveTyped and the restore it returns scope the typed locals to a branch of the generated code."] [689 1 "// tatom is a Go expression of type t ('I', 'W', 'D') of an atom's value, as hs.AotI, AotW, AotD convert it."] [698 4 "// an address of this process: read from the node (atom's generic path)"] [719 1 "// fn makes e's code a function of its own and is its name."] [730 1 "// atom is a Go expression of an atom's value."] [749 1 "// goLit is a literal as a Go constant expression of its Value, when it is a number and no address of this process (a"] [750 1 "// string literal's, a label's: another run's addresses differ; such a literal is read from its node)."] [768 1 "// aotNo (HSI_AOT_NO=Kind,...: App, CaseE, LetE, ...): node kinds left to the interpreter (a bisection's)."] [777 1 "// aotInline are the pure primops written inline: their Go over the arguments' typed expressions (aotOps: the"] [778 1 "// arguments' type and the result's, 'I' int64, 'W' uint64, 'D' float64), each Double# result an explicit float64"] [779 1 "// conversion so Go cannot fuse it."] [807 1 "// typedVal is a typed Go expression of an inline primop's value and its type, or \"\"."] [820 1 "// primVal is a Go expression of a pure primop's value, or \"\" when the primop is not pure (the node evaluates)."] [828 2 "// the machine's buffer, as PrimE.simple: an inline function literal fills it"] [839 1 "// expr is the statements of e in a tail position: they end in a return of the next code."] [901 3 "// FFIE, Unimpl: the node itself"] [908 1 "// clears are a call's or an entry's clearings once its arguments are read: the slots it kills, and the activation's"] [909 1 "// locals from clr in its tail position (live.go)"] [919 1 "// app is a call: its atoms read into the machine's argument buffer, App.eval's paths taken by aotApp."] [933 3 "// a known callee: resolved once at the call site (HES73)"] [948 3 "// the join point's body: compiled once, put in the join's place (the interpreter's jumps go there too)"] [1048 2 "// a scrutinee that never pushes the case's frame (a pure primop, a literal): the alternatives inline; an inline"] [1049 2 "// primop's value in a typed Go local (HES73), its binder's slot written to env only when env is read"] [1090 1 "// cont is the body of a case's continuation: the alternative chosen for the value in the return registers."] [1174 1 "// contTyped is the continuation of a case of kind prim on an inline primop's value, held in the typed local r of type t:"] [1175 1 "// its binder a typed local, a switch on integer literals over r itself, the other cases as cont on r boxed."]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[55 55] [65 38] [93 24] [254 24] [263 36] [270 26] [311 55] [321 25] [345 26] [357 37] [374 24] [383 25] [407 23] [414 24] [421 25] [439 22] [451 20] [474 44] [474 68] [495 52] [516 55] [519 86] [529 20] [589 26] [618 20] [626 24] [692 31] [697 29] [734 31] [742 28] [752 24] [788 13] [788 27] [822 26] [871 23] [1050 30] [1051 28] [1063 26] [1079 30] [1138 30] [1181 28]]} (go/file "aot.go" :imports [

    ;; AOT (HE8, doc/haskell/HASKELL-EVAL-SURVEY.md, "As built: HE8 (write-ahead)"): a module's STG compiled to Go over
    ;; this machine. The generator (GenAOT) compiles each top-level closure of the program's modules as hsi does
    ;; (compile.go's slots, join points and liveness) and writes its node tree as Go: one Go function per closure body,
    ;; per case continuation and per join point, each a function of the frame returning the next code to run (the
    ;; machine's trampoline: runSlice's loop), atoms read from their slots, the frequent pure primops inline, a case
    ;; on a constructor or a literal a chain of comparisons or a switch, a let's allocations inline. The generated
    ;; file is part of package hs in the program's build (bin/hsi aot-build): its init registers each closure's
    ;; installer by the module's key and the closure's name, with the shape of the tree it was generated from. At run
    ;; time the closure is compiled from its STG as before (the slice keeps the dumps: the declarations, the
    ;; constructors and the globals come from them) and the installer puts the Go code in place of the tree's code:
    ;; the closure's body, its nested closures' bodies and its join points' bodies become goCode, its cases' frames
    ;; continue in Go (CaseE.k), the tree itself kept for the collector's walks (rts.go) and for the nodes the
    ;; generator leaves to the interpreter (calls, entries, foreign calls). A shape that differs (another dump, another
    ;; compiler) refuses the installer: the closure runs interpreted.


